eptum morphology, abnormal cardiac ventricular function, abnormal cerebral white matter morphology\n  Favours second: abnormality of the ribs, arthralgia, edema, emg abnormality, muscle spasm\n\nIschemic Cerebrovascular Disease vs Thoracic Outlet Syndrome:\n  Favours first:  abnormal bleeding, abnormal cardiac ventricular function, abnormal cornea morphology, abnormal cutaneous elastic fiber morphology, abnormal facial shape\n  Favours second: abnormality of the ribs, arthralgia, edema, emg abnormality, muscle spasm\n\nRelated to Malignant Neoplasm of the Thoracic Apices: esophageal cancer\n\nRelated to Brachial Plexus Injury or Compression: brachial plexus neuropathy\n\nRelated to Ischemic Cerebrovascular Disease: brain ischemia, ischemic bowel disease, limb ischemia\n\nRelated to Thoracic Outlet Syndrome: arterial thoracic outlet syndrome, neurogenic thoracic outlet syndrome, syndromic disease\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\n  A 55-year-old male bodybuilder presents to the emergency department with weakness of his right arm → hyporeflexia of upper limbs → Brachial Plexus Injury or Compression"}
